{"notes": "I couldn't do this research, so I have no commentary notes to give you.\n\nMy first set of searches ran, but the results came back in a form my script didn't expect. When I tried again to read them, I'd hit the limit on search tool calls for this turn. That means I haven't read a single page from enduringword.com, biblehub.com, studylight.org, preceptaustin.org, netbible.org or any other site on your list. You asked me to report only what pages say, give a URL for every point and not fill gaps from my own knowledge, so I haven't written any verse notes. Anything I wrote now would come from memory, not from the sources.\n\nIf you ask again in a new message, I can do it properly. I'd plan to:\n1. **Read verse-by-verse sources:** Enduring Word on Jeremiah 51, and the Bible Hub and StudyLight pages for Gill, Ellicott, the Pulpit Commentary and Barnes on verses 1–21. I'd also check Precept Austin.\n2. **Look up particular points:** the name \"Leb-kamai\" (v. 1), the gold cup (v. 7), \"vengeance for His temple\" and the Medes (v. 11), how verses 15–19 echo Jeremiah 10:12–16, and the war club (vv. 20–21). Commentators disagree on whether the club is Babylon, Cyrus or Israel.\n3. **Find other views:** the NET Bible notes, and Catholic or Orthodox readings from New Advent or OCA. I'd look for differences between Protestant traditions or popular modern teaching only where the sites actually discuss them.\n\nEvery point would come with its URL.", "urls": ["https://bible.org/seriespage/jeremiah-51", "https://biblehub.com/commentaries/jeremiah/51-1.htm", "https://biblehub.com/commentaries/jeremiah/51-11.htm", "https://biblehub.com/commentaries/jeremiah/51-20.htm", "https://biblehub.com/commentaries/jeremiah/51-51.htm", "https://biblehub.com/esv/jeremiah/51-11.htm", "https://biblehub.com/jeremiah/51-11.htm", "https://biblehub.com/jeremiah/51-20.htm", "https://biblehub.com/jeremiah/51-7.htm", "https://biblehub.com/kjv/jeremiah/51-11.htm", "https://biblehub.com/lexicon/j